Fix: streaming TTS aborts every LiveKit reply with "unsupported operand type(s) for -: 'float' and 'NoneType'"

Applies to (identical content, both must be patched or ExecStartPre re-applies the bug):
  /usr/local/lib/hermes-agent/venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/hermes_livekit/streaming_tts.py
  /root/projects/livekit-spike/patches/hermes_livekit_streaming_tts.py

Why: gateway/streaming_tts_consumer.py (hermes 0.21.3) marks handle.audible=True after the first
write_streaming_tts() even when it yielded zero frames, so the `if not handle.audible:` block that
sets first_queued_at never runs; the onset log then subtracts None. 17/17 replies aborted since
2026-09-13 21:03 UTC.

--- a/streaming_tts.py
+++ b/streaming_tts.py
@@ -150,7 +150,7 @@
                 handle.pending = None
             if not self._tts_current(handle):
                 return
-            if not handle.audible:
+            if handle.first_queued_at is None:
                 handle.first_queued_at = time.monotonic()
                 trimmed_ms = handle.leading_silence.trimmed_frames * 20 if handle.leading_silence else 0
                 logger.info("[%s] streaming TTS first PCM: %.3fs from stream open; trimmed=%dms",
@@ -166,7 +166,7 @@
                     "[%s] streaming TTS non-quiet PCM: response_id=%s offset_samples=%d "
                     "offset=%.3fs queued=%.3fs from first PCM; %.3fs from stream open; peak>%d",
                     handle.chat_id, handle.response_id, onset, onset / OUTPUT_RATE,
-                    now - handle.first_queued_at, now - handle.opened_at, PCM_ONSET_PEAK,
+                    now - (handle.first_queued_at or now), now - handle.opened_at, PCM_ONSET_PEAK,
                 )

Apply (on CT116, after Drew's OK, then restart):
  P=/usr/local/lib/hermes-agent/venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/hermes_livekit/streaming_tts.py
  S=/root/projects/livekit-spike/patches/hermes_livekit_streaming_tts.py
  for f in $P $S; do
    cp -a $f $f.bak-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)
    sed -i 's/^            if not handle.audible:$/            if handle.first_queued_at is None:/' $f
    sed -i 's/now - handle.first_queued_at, now - handle.opened_at, PCM_ONSET_PEAK,/now - (handle.first_queued_at or now), now - handle.opened_at, PCM_ONSET_PEAK,/' $f
  done
  python3 -m py_compile $P && systemctl restart hermes-livekit-spike

Verify: journalctl -u hermes-livekit-spike -f | grep -E "streaming TTS (finished|clause)"  → aborted=False
